{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PARTIALLY DELIVERED — change ade954fcd3 landed on main; this ticket stays OPEN.\n\nLANDED: the self-healing AC only. gitutil.path_is_foreign_to_branch + discard_unmerged_paths,\nwired into event_append._recover_from_unmerged as a third bucket. A stranded index caused by\npaths the tickets branch does not track now HEALS instead of wedging every store write.\n\nNOT LANDED — the PRIMARY AC of this ticket:\n  _store/push.py STILL performs the stash -> merge -> pop dance in the tickets worktree\n  (module docstring line 9; _resolve_conflicted_pop lines 167-200; 'stash drop' at line 200).\nAlso outstanding: the maintenance entrypoint, the break-glass, and the fsck invariant that\nreports a tracker containing tracked-source paths.\n\nRESIDUAL RISK (the reason this must not be closed):\nThe incident needed two conditions — (1) rebar stashes in the tickets worktree, and (2) the\nstash stack contains a foreign stash. Condition 1 is STILL TRUE EVERYWHERE. Condition 2 is now\nimpossible ON THIS MACHINE ONLY, because .tickets-tracker was converted to a standalone clone.\nAny other environment whose tracker is still a LINKED WORKTREE — which was the default setup\nhere — retains both conditions. The reviewbot is safe (Dockerfile.reviewbot:154 clones), but\nother developer machines and CI checkouts have not been audited.\n\nWhat the landed change buys everywhere: the OUTAGE is prevented (self-heal) even where the\nCAUSE remains. Only the pollution still occurs.\n\nSUBTLETY to preserve if the auto-discard is ever revisited: discarding foreign paths deletes\nfiles that, in this incident, were a colleague's RECOVERED ADR-0061 work. That is safe ONLY\nbecause 'git stash pop' KEEPS the stash entry when it conflicts (verified experimentally:\n'The stash entry is kept in case you need it again'), so the source of truth survives and only\nthe applied copy is removed. If that ever ceased to hold, auto-discard would become data loss.\n\nSuggested order for the remainder: (1) remove the stash from push.py, (2) fsck invariant so a\npolluted tracker is REPORTED rather than silently healed, (3) maintenance entrypoint +\nbreak-glass."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786375380635485001,"uuid":"aba64da5-5b30-4de3-8d64-32683b26e4af"}